{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5344d80-9664-403c-b2ff-b16d321a832e","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The rectangle contains every possible outcome. The circle is event A: all outcomes where A happens.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The complement of an event"},{"op":"figure","id":"venn","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.3,8.3],"y":[-0.3,5.3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"sample_space","points":[[0,0],[8,0],[8,5],[0,5]],"closed":true},{"kind":"circle","id":"event_a","center":[2.8,2.5],"r":1.6},{"kind":"text","at":[2.8,3.3],"text":"A"},{"kind":"text","at":[7.5,4.5],"text":"S"}]},{"op":"text","id":"space_note","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"S: all possible outcomes"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5344d80-9664-403c-b2ff-b16d321a832e","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The complement of A is everything inside the rectangle but outside the circle. It means A does not happen.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"shade_comp","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"shade","inside":"sample_space","except":["event_a"]},{"kind":"text","at":[6,2.8],"text":"Aᶜ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"complement","anchor":{"el":"space_note","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"A^c=S\\setminus A"},{"op":"text","id":"not_a","anchor":{"el":"complement","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"Shaded region: A does not happen"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f5344d80-9664-403c-b2ff-b16d321a832e","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A and its complement cover every outcome without overlapping. Their probabilities add to one, so subtract the probability of A to find its complement.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"prob_rule","anchor":{"el":"not_a","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(A^c)=1-P(A)"},{"op":"figure","id":"prob_labels","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[2.8,2.3],"text":"0.3"},{"kind":"text","at":[6,2],"text":"0.7"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"prob_rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(A)=0.3\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad P(A^c)=0.7"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Can an outcome belong to both A and its complement?","expected_gist":"No; A and its complement do not overlap."}}}
